  "findings": [
    "All four WRF DATA.json coefficient files are byte-identical (SHA-256) to the files in rrtmgp-data@ea788bb.",
    "The pinned upstream source compiles, but its unmodified all-sky example loader cannot read the pinned cloud files: it asks for radice_lwr and later LUT names, while the current data files expose diamice_lwr/diamice_upr and extliq/ssaliq/asyliq (and corresponding ice fields). The run stops with read_field: cannot find variable radice_lwr. WRF SOURCE.json records local reader adaptations for these renamed fields and diameter coordinates.",
    "The published all-sky reference outputs are Garand-example cases with 24 columns and 72 layers. The upstream example driver uses g256/g224 gas distributions and g-point cloud files; its reference files therefore do not match WRF g128/g112 gas coefficients or the band-cloud inputs/actual WRF columns.",
    "Official RFMIP example inputs/reference outputs are also available in the pinned data repo; upstream driver uses g256/g224. They are a valid upstream code/data regression set at that resolution, not a direct comparison target for WRF g128/g112."
  ],
